# Plano punto-normal (T031 - MED-04.06-V)

Plano definido por un punto $P_0$ y un vector normal $\mathbf{n}$.
La ecuación es $\mathbf{n} \cdot (\mathbf{X} - \mathbf{P}_0) = 0$.

```plane3d
id: plane3d-point-normal
mode: point-normal
point: [1, 2, 3]
normal: [2, -1, 1]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-5, 5]
yDomain: [-5, 5]
color: "#6366f1"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano punto-normal
labelPoint: P₀
labelNormal: n
```

La ecuación general es $2x - y + z - 3 = 0$. Los interceptos son $x = 1.5$, $y = -3$, $z = 3$.

---

## Plano ecuación general (T033 - MED-04.07-V)

Plano definido por la ecuación general $Ax + By + Cz + D = 0$.

```plane3d
id: plane3d-general
mode: general
A: 2
B: -1
C: 1
D: -3
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-5, 5]
yDomain: [-5, 5]
color: "#8b5cf6"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano ecuación general
labelPoint: P₀
labelNormal: n
```

Equivale al plano $2x - y + z = 3$ con interceptos $x = 1.5$, $y = -3$, $z = 3$.

---

## Plano 3 puntos (T035 - MED-04.08-V)

Plano definido por tres puntos no colineales $A$, $B$, $C$.
La normal es $\mathbf{n} = (\mathbf{B} - \mathbf{A}) \times (\mathbf{C} - \mathbf{A})$.

```plane3d
id: plane3d-three-points
mode: three-points
pointA: [1, 0, 0]
pointB: [0, 2, 0]
pointC: [0, 0, 3]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-2, 4]
yDomain: [-2, 4]
color: "#ec4899"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano 3 puntos
labelPoint: A
labelNormal: n = AB × AC
```

Los puntos $A(1,0,0)$, $B(0,2,0)$, $C(0,0,3)$ definen el plano $\frac{x}{1} + \frac{y}{2} + \frac{z}{3} = 1$ o $6x + 3y + 2z = 6$.

---

## Plano punto + 2 vectores (T037 - MED-04.09-V)

Plano definido por un punto $P$ y dos vectores generadores $\mathbf{u}$, $\mathbf{v}$.
La normal es $\mathbf{n} = \mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v}$.
Ecuación paramétrica: $\mathbf{X} = \mathbf{P} + s\mathbf{u} + t\mathbf{v}$.

```plane3d
id: plane3d-point-vectors
mode: point-vectors
point: [1, 1, 1]
vectorU: [2, 0, 0]
vectorV: [0, 2, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-2, 4]
yDomain: [-2, 4]
color: "#14b8a6"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano P + u, v
labelPoint: P
labelU: u
labelV: v
labelNormal: n = u × v
```

Plano horizontal $z = 1$ con vectores $\mathbf{u} = (2,0,0)$, $\mathbf{v} = (0,2,0)$.

---

## Plano paramétrico (T039 - MED-04.10-V)

Mismo que punto-vectores pero enfocado en la parametrización $\mathbf{X} = \mathbf{P} + s\mathbf{u} + t\mathbf{v}$.

```plane3d
id: plane3d-parametric
mode: parametric
point: [0, 0, 0]
vectorU: [2, 1, 0]
vectorV: [-1, 2, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#f97316"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano paramétrico
labelPoint: P
labelU: u
labelV: v
labelNormal: n
```

Plano $z = 0$ con malla paramétrica generada por $\mathbf{u} = (2,1,0)$ y $\mathbf{v} = (-1,2,0)$.

---

## Planos paralelos y perpendiculares (T041 - MED-04.11-V)

Dos planos con normales $\mathbf{n}_1$ y $\mathbf{n}_2$.
- Paralelos: $\mathbf{n}_1 \times \mathbf{n}_2 = \mathbf{0}$
- Perpendiculares: $\mathbf{n}_1 \cdot \mathbf{n}_2 = 0$

```plane3d
id: plane3d-parallel
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [1, 1, 1]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-5, 5]
yDomain: [-5, 5]
color: "#3b82f6"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano 1 (n₁)
labelPoint: P₁
labelNormal: n₁
---
plane3d
id: plane3d-perpendicular
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [1, -1, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-5, 5]
yDomain: [-5, 5]
color: "#ef4444"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano 2 (n₂)
labelPoint: P₂
labelNormal: n₂
```

Plano 1: $x + y + z = 0$, Plano 2: $x - y = 0$. $\mathbf{n}_1 \cdot \mathbf{n}_2 = 0$ → perpendiculares.

---

## Intersección recta-plano (T043 - MED-04.12-V)

Recta $\mathbf{r}(t) = \mathbf{P} + t\mathbf{v}$ intersectando plano $\mathbf{n} \cdot (\mathbf{X} - \mathbf{P}_0) = 0$.

```line3d
id: line-plane-intersection
point: [0, 0, 0]
direction: [1, 0, 0]
tDomain: [-3, 3]
showPoint: true
showDirection: true
color: "#3b82f6"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorDirection: "#f59e0b"
labelPoint: P
labelDirection: v
label: Recta r(t)
---
plane3d
id: plane3d-line-intersection
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [1, 1, 1]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#3b82f6"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano x+y+z=0
labelPoint: P₀
labelNormal: n
```

Recta $x$-eje intersecta plano $x+y+z=0$ en $(\frac{1}{3}, \frac{1}{3}, \frac{1}{3})$.

---

## Intersección dos planos (T045 - MED-04.13-V)

Dos planos se intersectan en una recta (si no son paralelos).

```plane3d
id: plane3d-intersect-1
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [1, 0, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#3b82f6"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano 1: x=0 (yz-plano)
labelPoint: P₁
labelNormal: n₁
---
plane3d
id: plane3d-intersect-2
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [0, 1, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
showIntercepts: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#ef4444"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Plano 2: y=0 (xz-plano)
labelPoint: P₂
labelNormal: n₂
```

Plano 1: $x=0$ (plano $yz$), Plano 2: $y=0$ (plano $xz$). Se intersectan en el eje $z$ (recta $x=0, y=0$).

---

## Intersección tres planos (T047 - MED-04.14-V)

Tres planos pueden intersectarse en un punto, una recta, un plano o conjunto vacío.

```plane3d
id: three-planes-1
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [1, 0, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#3b82f6"
label: Plano 1: x=0
---
plane3d
id: three-planes-2
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [0, 1, 0]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#ef4444"
label: Plano 2: y=0
---
plane3d
id: three-planes-3
mode: point-normal
point: [0, 0, 0]
normal: [0, 0, 1]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#22c55e"
label: Plano 3: z=0
```

Tres planos coordenados $x=0$, $y=0$, $z=0$ se intersectan en el origen $(0,0,0)$.

---

## Caso degenerado: 3 puntos colineales (T036 - MED-04.08-C)

```plane3d
id: plane3d-degenerate
mode: three-points
pointA: [0, 0, 0]
pointB: [1, 1, 1]
pointC: [2, 2, 2]
origin: [0, 0, 0]
showPoint: true
showNormal: true
xDomain: [-3, 3]
yDomain: [-3, 3]
color: "#ef4444"
colorPoint: "#10b981"
colorNormal: "#f59e0b"
opacity: 0.3
label: Puntos colineales (degenerado)
labelPoint: A
labelNormal: n
```

Los puntos $A(0,0,0)$, $B(1,1,1)$, $C(2,2,2)$ son colineales → no definen un plano único.